# AC-REC-01 verifier run 2026-11-09T03:17:00Z
$ capture --help
capture — play a live page in real time, drive it with a storyboard, and screen-capture it

Usage: capture --storyboard <file.mjs> --out <take.webm|.mp4> [options]   |   capture --plates plates.json --plate <id>

Three modes, one storyboard: silent (--no-captions), captions (default) and spine-timed (--spine,
or --plates/--plate). In spine-timed mode say() plays to the spine manifest's clip timing (no TTS
here), waitForVoice() waits for the clip's end, and the take lasts exactly the plate's (or the
spine's) planned duration. Otherwise say() holds for reading time (about 3 words/s, at least 1.5 s)
and the take ends when the storyboard returns and the last say() has finished.
The page is --url, else the plate's live.url, else the storyboard's exported `url`, else an
index.html next to the storyboard; local files are served on 127.0.0.1. Pre-flight (Chromium,
ffmpeg, the pinned Playwright, a valid --spine) runs before any browser opens.
Storyboard API: references/storyboard-api.md.

Options:
      --storyboard <file.mjs>   Storyboard module: export default async ({ page, say, waitForVoice, wait }) => { … }
      --out <file>              The take: .webm, .mkv or .mp4 (picture only) (default with --plate: <project>/renders/plates/<id>.mp4)
      --mp4 <file.mp4>          Also write an H.264/AAC MP4 with faststart (silent audio track)
      --viewport <WxH>          Browser viewport (default: the plate's live.viewport, else 1280x720)
      --no-captions             Draw no captions (silent mode without --spine)
      --caption-css <file.css>  Caption style sheet (classes .pm-caption-wrap, .pm-caption) replacing the neutral default
      --url <url|file>          Page to load: http(s) URL or local .html file/folder (overrides the plate and storyboard)
      --debug-requests          Log every page request, failure and HTTP error to stderr
      --audio-offset-ms <ms>    Audio placement offset. Spine-timed: say() fires at clip start minus this (default: the spine's audioOffsetMs); otherwise recorded for the mux (default: -100)
      --spine <manifest.json>   Spine manifest: say() plays to its clip timing (spine-timed mode)
      --plates <plates.json>    Project plate list; with --plate, supplies storyboard, url, viewport, fps, size, spine and the planned window
      --plate <id>              The live plate to capture (needs --plates)
      --fps <n>                 Capture frame rate (default: plates.json fps, else 30)
      --json                    Print the take summary as JSON
  -h, --help                    Show this help and exit
      --version                 Print the plugin version and exit

Examples:
  capture --storyboard examples/deck/storyboard.mjs --out /tmp/deck.webm
  capture --storyboard examples/deck/storyboard.mjs --out /tmp/deck.mp4 --no-captions
  capture --storyboard examples/deck/storyboard.mjs --out /tmp/deck.mp4 --spine spine/manifest.json
  capture --plates plates.json --plate r1-feature
exit=0

